{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0186X2ByrabmSx82D6wTLzCD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a **personal productivity / project-management system** built for one user (J.C. Liechty), with a recent R&D \"cockpit\" subsystem layered on top. Grounded in the project's own docs:\n\n**What it is**\n- A **single-folder, stdlib-only Python app** (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`, no external deps except an optional `pywinpty` for terminals) where **plain markdown files are the source of truth** â€” no database, no syncing.\n- It ships **`anchor_gui.py`** (the declared deliverable): a self-contained local HTTP server that renders a full task dashboard and writes changes back to markdown. It runs **persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`** on `http://localhost:8777`.\n\n**What it does â€” core productivity layer**\n- Manages tasks through a lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored) across domain files (`academic.md`, `commercial.md`, `family.md`, `writing.md`) plus `DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`.\n- Offers both a **browser GUI** (interactive checkboxes, add/capture/edit) and a **CLI mirror** (`anchor.py` â€” `done`, `add`, `capture`, `cancel`, `save`, etc.) that share the same markdown format.\n- Runs a **daily 5 AM health check** (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint, and writes a dated report.\n\n**What it does â€” R&D control surface (the major recent build)**\n- Adds a **per-project \"cockpit\"** for \"trio-driven R&D\" â€” the Research â†’ Planning â†’ Build skill pipeline (researchPrime / Crucible / Foreman).\n- Each project's window shows lanes as **status-lit tiles** (green/amber/red/grey) that expand **inline panels** with a cached summary on top and a **real, resizable ConPTY terminal below** (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket/SSE transport), with per-session **git-worktree isolation**.\n- Layers on: cached/validated session & project summaries, a session registry, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews (guarded off port 8777), an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini), cost/tokens/time rollups, and a grass-catcher idea board.\n- This evolved across four versioned waves (v1â†’v4 \"Project Cockpit\"), **all built and merged to master** (latest: v4, 637 tests passing).\n\nIn short: **a markdown-backed personal task dashboard that grew into a local mission-control for running and tracking AI-assisted R&D projects**, all served from one always-on local web app.\n\nThe working-tree currently has uncommitted changes (modified dashboards/domain files, new `.anchor/`, `rnd_jobs/`, `Anchor.md`) â€” let me know if you'd like a grounded read on what those pending changes represent."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fed477f3-3e6d-40cc-a137-985bb914ad9c","uuid":"d0ca3700-2529-477c-857f-1840f569a7b6","request_id":"req_011Cc1JJ22veNm5LV8zj8mX1"}
